This morning we have been incredibly busy.
I have just made my very first cappuccino.
A little before ten, a man came over to the counter.
"A cappuccino, please," he said.
I have just learned to use the espresso machine.
So I went over to the machine right away.
I brewed the coffee and put the steam wand down into the milk.
But I held it a little too deep down.
I have probably been a little too nervous.
Unfortunately, the milk did not get any thick foam.
I looked carefully down into the pitcher.
The foam was not completely perfect.
But it still looked acceptable.
I poured the hot milk over the coffee in the cup.
Then I gave the coffee to the man with a polite smile.
"Here you go, that will be fifty-five kroner," I said.
He took the cup and sat down at the first table.
He has looked happy ever since.
